      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Standard microelectrode techniques were used to study the impulse activity of different types of nodosal ganglion neurons. Differences in electrical activity of cardiovascular neurons were observed in myocardial ischemia both complicated and not complicated by fibrillation. In these conditions rhythmic activity of cardiopulmonary, late inspiratory and inspiratory-expiratory neurons is quite similar."},
